+     *
+     * Previously the code waited until 200 ms had accumulated and then
+     * recreated the whole PulseAudio stream.  Recreating the stream is
+     * expensive (it can glitch) and, more importantly, it lets up to those
+     * 200 ms of backlog reach the network first.  Drain the backlog in place
+     * instead, so at most one ~10 ms read slips through, and keep the stream
+     * alive.  g_pa_reading stays 1 to protect a concurrent pulse_stop. */
     if (!g_pa_stopping) {
         if (g_drift_skips > 0) {
